WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.429
If you sell chemistry, equipment or services into plants, this is how you sell with the plant's own numbers.

2
00:00:08.479 --> 00:00:10.417
You work in your own workspace.

3
00:00:10.417 --> 00:00:16.107
Load your product sheets once, and every match AquaMesh makes is quoted straight from them.

4
00:00:17.157 --> 00:00:19.649
Then find plants worth approaching.

5
00:00:19.649 --> 00:00:22.211
Say where, and what kinds of plants.

6
00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:32.961
It ranks real facilities from public EPA and energy records by how well they fit what you sell, with who signs, and an opening that credits their team.

7
00:00:34.011 --> 00:00:36.349
The approach: ask, don't tell.

8
00:00:36.349 --> 00:00:42.661
Ask for a few months of historian data, and give them the full report back, free.

9
00:00:42.661 --> 00:00:47.960
Here, Tule Ridge Dairy Foods, a fictional dairy with simulated data.

10
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.445
They share an export, and the audit starts in a chat.

11
00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:57.046
Upload what they sent, match it against your own documents, and run it.

12
00:00:57.046 --> 00:01:02.489
Two point oh three million dollars a year, on their own data, across eight findings.

13
00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:05.168
Your rep gets a brief:

14
00:01:05.168 --> 00:01:15.015
which findings your products address and how strongly, who decides, the questions to ask, the objections to expect, and a talk track.

15
00:01:15.015 --> 00:01:17.828
Every figure traces back to a finding.

16
00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:24.991
And the plant gets its own report, from its own records, including what you can't fix.

17
00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:26.767
That's what builds trust.

18
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:32.676
When they say yes, the same audit becomes a live digital twin.

19
00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:34.165
One chat builds it.

20
00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:42.294
The plan shows what it will watch, detect and predict, and every finding becomes value the twin tracks.

21
00:01:43.344 --> 00:01:46.662
It goes live only when every check passes.

22
00:01:47.712 --> 00:01:51.941
Here, on our demonstration plant, every unit runs live in 3D.

23
00:01:51.941 --> 00:02:00.538
When something goes wrong, it scores the possible responses, with safety as a hard gate, and walks the team through the fix.

24
00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:09.633
At Tule Ridge, the plant's gateway streams its historian data out to the twin, and every signal shows up as it arrives.

25
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:17.292
Detectors built from the audit watch the plant around the clock, and the team works each finding to closure.

26
00:02:18.342 --> 00:02:23.985
Anyone can ask the plant a question in plain words, and get an answer from its live data.

27
00:02:25.035 --> 00:02:30.991
And the audit's two million dollars is tracked, line by line, against measured savings.

28
00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:38.806
Models train on the plant's own history, and alerts reach Teams, Slack, email or a phone call.

29
00:02:39.856 --> 00:02:41.238
Advisory by default:

30
00:02:41.238 --> 00:02:45.107
nothing reaches the plant without a person approving it.

31
00:02:46.157 --> 00:02:50.023
Walk in with their numbers. Walk out with a next step.

